  "reportGiveCode": "Give this code to Support.",
  "reportFailedTitle": "Not sent",
  "@reportFailedTitle": {"description": "One sentence under it says why. When the server was not reached: reportFailedHelp; buttons retry (resends the same report and images) and cancelButton. When it answered without taking the report: reportFailedBusy or reportFailedRefused. When the server refused this device's clock: clockWrongTitle and clockWrongHelp in a red message, then dateSettings (primary) and retry."},
  "reportFailedHelp": "Check your internet and try again.",
  "@reportFailedHelp": {"description": "No answer at all: offline, timed out, or no door reached."},
  "reportFailedBusy": "Too many reports right now. Try again in an hour.",
  "@reportFailedBusy": {"description": "The server answered 429: six an hour per device, six per address before sign-in (a carrier may give one address to many phones), or 600 an hour in all. So it never says who sent them. The window is fixed, so an hour is the longest wait. Buttons as reportFailedRefused."},
  "reportFailedRefused": "The problem is on our side. Chat with Support on Telegram.",
  "@reportFailedRefused": {"description": "The server answered with any other status: 400, 413, 422, 5xx, or 200 without a code. Over HTTPS only our own server or its front gives such an answer, so the fault is ours. Retry resends the very same report, so a 4xx refuses it again; hence no «try later» here. Buttons: support (primary; on a phone it opens the chat, on TV its QR dialog without the report button) and retry. No cancelButton: back leaves, as on the clock state."},
